---
id: chicken-cheese-soup-with-croutons
title: Chicken Cheese Soup with Croutons
category: one_dish

yield:
  servings: 3
  cooked_g: 3150

storage:
  fridge_days: 3
  freezer_friendly: false

---

Pour @chicken-broth{2%package} into a #large-pot and bring to a boil. Add @white-boiling-potatoes{600%g}, peeled and cut into 2 cm cubes, plus @carrots{150%g}, peeled and left whole, @yellow-onion{1}, peeled and left whole, and @bay-leaves{2}. Simmer on medium heat for ~simmer-veg{10%min}.

Cut @boneless-chicken-breast{1%package} into bite-size pieces and add them to the pot. Season with @kosher-salt{1/2%tsp}, @black-pepper{1/4%tsp} and @garlic-powder{1/2%tsp}; the croutons are salty, so taste before adding more. Simmer gently for ~simmer-chicken{12%min}, skimming off the foam, until the chicken is cooked through and a knife slides easily into the carrots.

Take the pot off the heat. Lift out the carrots, onion and bay leaves; throw away the bay leaves. Blend the carrots and onion with a ladle of broth in a #blender until smooth, then stir the purée back into the soup.

Whisk in @brick-cream-cheese{6%tbsp}, a spoonful at a time, until fully melted. Cover and let the soup rest for ~rest{10%min}, then divide it between 3 containers.

At serving time, reheat a portion and top it with a third of the bag of @cheese-garlic-croutons{1%package}. Keep the croutons in their bag, not in the soup, so they stay crisp.
